-Modern implementations, such as those found in differentiable tomography libraries, often automate camera parameter computation. Given a bounding box, direction, and distance, the system computes the eye position, target, and field of view (FOV) to generate rays for both perspective and parallel projections [S3, unofficial]. The FOV is typically defined vertically in degrees, with defaults around 60 degrees [S3, unofficial].
